From: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:44:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LU-21030 ldiskfs: allow MDT file size above maxbytes

Allow a regular file inode to have i_size beyond maxbytes.

Linux 6.16 commit 1a77a028a392 ("ext4: ensure i_size is smaller
than maxbytes") rejects such an inode as corrupt. A Lustre MDT
inode records the size of file data held on OSTs or in an HSM
archive, which can exceed the MDT's maxbytes, and the MDT is
remounted read-only on the first lookup of such a file.

---
 fs/ext4/inode.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/ext4/inode.c b/fs/ext4/inode.c
--- a/fs/ext4/inode.c
+++ b/fs/ext4/inode.c
@@ -5304,7 +5304,9 @@ struct inode *__ext4_iget(struct super_block *sb, unsigned long ino,
 			((__u64)le16_to_cpu(raw_inode->i_file_acl_high)) << 32;
 	inode->i_size = ext4_isize(sb, raw_inode);
 	size = i_size_read(inode);
-	if (size < 0 || size > ext4_get_maxbytes(inode)) {
+	/* a Lustre MDT inode can record the size of data held elsewhere */
+	if (size < 0 ||
+	    (!S_ISREG(inode->i_mode) && size > ext4_get_maxbytes(inode))) {
 		ext4_error_inode(inode, function, line, 0,
 				 "iget: bad i_size value: %lld", size);
 		ret = -EFSCORRUPTED;
